  "body": "﻿## What changed\r\n\r\nThe provider Test control now shows a distinct \"key rejected\" status when a\r\ncloud provider rejects the key, instead of one shared failure text.\r\n\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/ai_chat/settings_text.rs`: a new `is_auth_failure`\r\n  rule classifies the authentication failure before the generic status match.\r\n  The rule is:\r\n  - HTTP 401 or 403: authentication failure, for every cloud provider behind\r\n    Test (Anthropic, OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses, Gemini).\r\n  - Any other status: key rejected only when the provider error carries one of\r\n    its documented classified auth fields: `authentication_error` (Anthropic\r\n    `error.type`), `invalid_api_key` (OpenAI `error.code`), `api_key_invalid`\r\n    or `UNAUTHENTICATED` (Gemini `error.status`), or Gemini's documented plain\r\n    message \"API key not valid\". Gemini answers a bad key with HTTP 400, not\r\n    401; without this shape Gemini would show the generic request failure.\r\n  - The status line reads `Test failed: the key was rejected (HTTP <code>).`\r\n    The provider response text is never shown beyond the already redacted\r\n    classified fields, and the key is removed before any of this runs\r\n    (`http.rs` redacts before truncation, unchanged).\r\n- Other failures keep their own statuses, distinct from key rejected: wrong\r\n  model (404 or 400/422 without an auth marker), billing or credits (402 or a\r\n  billing marker), rate limit (429), provider outage (5xx), network, and an\r\n  invalid Model name.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/ai_http_review.rs`: pin that each provider's transport\r\n  surfaces the HTTP authentication status and never the key.\r\n\r\n## Classification note (conservative cases)\r\n\r\nHTTP 403 can also mean a permission or region denial, not a bad key. The rule\r\nstill reports key rejected for 403: the hint (\"paste a new key\") names the\r\nmost common cause, and no provider here returns 403 for a credit or model\r\nfailure. A 400 is only key rejected through the documented marker, never\r\nguessed, so a wrong model on Gemini stays a model failure.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `egui_app::tests::ai_chat::settings_failure_details::authentication_failure_shows_key_rejected_for_each_cloud_provider`\r\n- `egui_app::tests::ai_chat::settings_failure_details::gemini_bad_request_with_documented_key_error_shows_key_rejected`\r\n- `egui_app::tests::ai_chat::settings_failure_details::non_auth_cloud_test_failures_remain_distinct_from_key_rejected`\r\n- `egui_app::tests::ai_chat::settings_hand_test::failed_test_names_the_cause_the_model_and_what_to_try` (updated wording)\r\n- `authentication_failure_surfaces_the_http_status_for_each_cloud_provider` (`camcraft-app`, `ai_http_review`)\r\n\r\n## Gate\r\n\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test ai_http_review`: 7 passed.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib`: 307 passed.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 1612 passed, 8 ignored.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\nThe live-ai lane (#3803) does not exist yet. Its wrong-key step (\"Use a wrong\r\nkey and confirm the key rejected status\") is already specified there and was\r\nnot run here; every pin above runs over loopback HTTP fixtures, not real\r\ncredentials or remote services. The Gemini 400 marker path is pinned from the\r\npublished API error shape, not from a live provider answer.\r\n\r\nChangelog: AI Chat: the provider Test shows a key rejected status after an authentication failure, with other causes kept distinct.\r\n\r\nFixes #3804\r\n\r\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe provider Test status for a Gemini key rejection (HTTP 400 with the documented key-error reason). Before: bare main shows the generic request-refused line. After: this branch classifies the documented reason field and shows the key-rejected line with the key-replacement hint.\n\nBefore (bare main):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3924-key-rejected-before.png)\n\nAfter (this branch):\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr3924-key-rejected-after.png)\n\r\n",
